From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] single player: let console commands reach the game module

Cmd_ExecuteString offers a command to the game module only while com_sv_running is set. The
single-player bridge hosts the module without a running server, so the flag is never set there and
the module's own commands (nav, npc, runscript, ICARUS, ...) cannot be reached from the console,
a config or the UI -- only `use`, which the bridge registers by hand. SV_GameCommand already
forwards to the SP module when asked; this asks it whenever the SP game is active.

Independent of Long Way Home: it restores the released game's developer commands in this port.
---
diff --git a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/efcode/qcommon/cmd.c b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/efcode/qcommon/cmd.c
--- a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/efcode/qcommon/cmd.c
+++ b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/efcode/qcommon/cmd.c
@@ -800,8 +800,14 @@
 	}
 
 	// check server game commands
-	if ( com_sv_running && com_sv_running->integer && SV_GameCommand() ) {
-		return;
+	// The single-player bridge hosts the game module without a running server, so com_sv_running is
+	// never set there and the module's own console commands (nav, npc, runscript, ...) were unreachable.
+	// SV_GameCommand already knows how to hand a command to the SP module; let it be asked.
+	{
+		extern int SP_IsActive( void );
+		if ( ( ( com_sv_running && com_sv_running->integer ) || SP_IsActive() ) && SV_GameCommand() ) {
+			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	// check ui commands
